{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 confirmed root cause: all seven listed fixtures copy the complete insertion-ordered `os.environ` into a subprocess mapping and return that mapping directly or nested in a rendered box. On an unrelated assertion failure, pytest default long traceback renders the fixture/test argument with `saferepr`, so arbitrary inherited values early enough in the mapping enter test output. Changeable sites: materialize_probe.py:91, fetch_secrets.py:102, disk_pressure.py:107, health_gate.py:118, signals_gerrit_config.py:87, observability_exit.py:68, and interfaces/facades/test_cli.py:46. Runtime discriminant: with `SIBLING_TRACE_SECRET=TOP_SECRET_XIPHO` inserted first, an in-memory plugin forced an unrelated failure only after each real shipped test returned. All five autodeploy surfaces plus observability produced long traceback rc=1 with sentinel count=1, while the same tests under `--tb=short` produced rc=1 with sentinel count=0. For CLI, `_cli` was replaced in-memory so no child ran; long still rendered `offline_acli_env` with the sentinel and short did not. This rules out bash/CLI stdout or stderr as the carrier. A complete 24-test run under `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` passed, rejecting any behavioral requirement for arbitrary ambient inheritance. Required allowlists are: fake-bin-first PATH plus STATE_DIR/DEPLOY_REPO/COMPOSE_DIR/MIRROR_DIR for materialize/fetch/signals/disk; the same plus HEALTH_TIMEOUT=1 for health; PATH plus six explicit offset/log paths for observability; PATH only for CLI, with REBAR_ROOT added by its consumer and Jira credentials absent by construction. Per-case mappings remain mutable. Historical blame shows seven independent feature commits, proving a repeated harness construct rather than one regression commit. Legitimacy: defect, anchored by the landed parent contract `test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py` and commit 034e17209c, plus this ticket AC. Caller sweep found only the cited subprocess/helpers; none enumerates or depends on arbitrary keys, and the minimal-env run is dynamic proof all callers are incidental. Expected repair is an allowlisted mutable mapping preserving fake PATH and explicit overrides while omitting unrelated ambient values."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787032074993125001,"uuid":"1cb3f6cd-9ad7-4891-9a22-b84f944df3b2"}